{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A tenth I will tithe to You.</b> Jacob fulfilled his words, for he gave to HaShem a tithe of all that he had, and even of the children — for thus we find in the twelve tribes that were his: Ephraim and Menasseh, concerning whom it is written ״כראובן ושמעון יהיו לי״ — they are fourteen. Remove from them four firstborns for the four mothers, since the firstborn is consecrated and consecration does not remove the status of consecration — ten remain, and the tenth is the tribe of Levi, whom HaShem set apart to serve Him and to bless in His name. And this is what the Torah merited for him — the tithe. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived from this verse: one who distributes should not distribute more than a fifth, lest he come to need the support of others — for behold, one who separated from his property two tithes, and the second tithe as the first, behold this is a fifth of the property."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase ועשורא בתרא כי קמא is Aramaic (\"the second tithe as the first\"); rendered literally. The closing reasoning compresses the arithmetic of two tenths equaling one fifth."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:01.419080797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}